Z||000002||DRH||01-06-2000||03:26 PM||||Also, ground strap to the decklid???||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bill Osmer||01-06-2000||03:44 PM||||A quick way to tell is look if the trunk light comes on... If it does, then the connector (by the hinge) is back together. BTW, the ground strap to the decklid is only for RF shielding, not for electrical path. Look for the connector and any broken or cut wires, by the hinge (on my Fieor, the connector is on the passenger's side hinge)||||reg||1
Z||000004||ka4nkf||01-06-2000||09:49 PM||||You might check under the dash on the passenger side and see if the relay is pluged in good. The horn relay will also work for the trunk, it is just a little more heavy built.||||reg||1
